# Normalize everything to LF inside the repository.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks files out with
# CRLF and converts them back on commit. That is harmless but noisy, and it
# matters here for one reason: jsDelivr serves the bytes that are in the repo.
# Pinning LF keeps the CDN build byte-identical to what CI tested.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary

# The built bundles are committed on purpose — jsDelivr serves straight from a
# GitHub tag, so dist/ has to be in the tag. Marking it generated keeps it out
# of diffs and language statistics.
dist/** linguist-generated=true -diff
